sec.p:
The study enrolled 100 subjects, namely 60 MND patients with confirmed diagnosis and 40 age-matched controls. Demographic and clinical characteristics, as well as CSF biomarkers distribution are highlighted in Table 1 and Fig. 1. Motor neuron disease patients exhibited higher levels of GFAP, NfL, phosphorylated tau and total tau (p-Tau 181 and t-Tau) compared to HC. Levels of the synaptic protein CAP2 were higher in MND compared to HC whereas levels of SNAP-25 protein did not differ between MND and HC. At baseline, ALSFRS-R and DPR did not correlate with CAP2, SNAP-25, or any other CSF biomarker; only ALSFRS-R showed significant correlations with NfL and t-Tau.Table 1
Demographics and CSF biomarkers for HC and MND. Continuous variables are reported as median (IQR), and categorical variables are reported as numbers and percentages (n, %).
